course: dictionary
lesson: 4530
title: Health: how well you are
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Health is a noun, and it means how well your body and mind are working, free from illness and injury. When you meet it, read the words around it to see which meaning fits. «Some people eat meat; vegetarians and vegans do not, for reasons of animal welfare, health, the environment or religion.» Here health is a reason for a choice, so it is about keeping your body well.
explain: Health can also mean the state of your body at a given time. «Smoking is very bad for health.» The words bad for show that health can be good or bad. Health can also name the work of keeping people well, as in health care and health services.
explain: Look at the words next to health to decide. «In the UK your first stop for most health problems is the GP, the family doctor.» Health problems are things that make you ill, so the meaning is about the body, not a job or a place. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense?
fact: Health means how well your body and mind are working, free from illness and injury.
fact: «Health care» and «health services» are the work of keeping people well.
fact: «Health and safety» means the rules that keep people from getting hurt.
fact: «Mental health» means how well your mind and feelings are doing.
fact: The health of a business or a forest means how strong and well it is doing.
exercise: Ben eats fruit, sleeps well and brushes his teeth to look after his health. What does health mean here? | A kind of fruit | A place where you see a doctor | A school bus | *How well his body and mind are working
exercise: «The health centre is open on Saturday morning.» What does health mean in health centre? | A swimming pool | *A place where people are kept well and treated | A shop that sells vegetables | A park for running
exercise: «Mental health» is about your feelings. What does mental health mean? | How fast you can run | How tall you are | *How well your mind and feelings are doing | How many books you have read
test: After her illness she is in good health again. What does good health mean here? | *Her body and mind are well again | She has gone on holiday | She has no shoes | She is very rich
test: The health of the forest is poor after the fire. What does health mean here? | How big the forest is | *How strong and well the forest is doing | How many trees grow there | The number of animals in it
exam: Which phrase names the work of keeping people well? | *Health care | Health and safety | Healthy food | In good health
